      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm.  I see what you\u0027re going for.  But HASH_GET doesn\u0027t currently pay attention to p-\u003eoffset, and ectool doesn\u0027t even initialize it in cmd_ec_hash().  So this change will break existing ectool.\n\nI think we can make it work reverse-compatibly if we define that *only* the two special values EC_VBOOT_HASH_OFFSET_RO and EC_VBOOT_HASH_OFFSET_RW are checked.  If one of those is passed as p-\u003eoffset, then a hash will only be returned if it matches.  If any other value is passed for p-\u003eoffset, then it will be ignored.\n\nEither that, or the host needs to be responsible for checking r-\u003eoffset vs. the expected one.  (If it has a way of doing so...)",
